<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  profiletool's OWN HDR ColorSpace Profile fixture — a CONFORMING member of the
  HDR ColorSpace Profile sub-class of ICC.1 clause 8.7.1.

  Why this exists — AND HOW THAT CHANGED. It was written when every fixture copied
  from iccDEV:Testing/HDR/ carried the redTRCTag/greenTRCTag/blueTRCTag trio, which
  the then-current clause 8.10.1 said "shall not be present"; all of them therefore
  classified as icHdrProfileHdrContent, PAWG emitted H1 as N/A and suppressed the
  rest of the section, and no upstream fixture could exercise section H past its
  first item. The 23-09-2026 revision removed that prohibition along with the
  matrix/TRC parent class, and upstream's corpus now holds 25 conforming members.
  SO THE ORIGINAL JUSTIFICATION HAS LAPSED, and saying so is the honest thing to
  record rather than quietly restating a reason that no longer holds.

  What still earns its keep is the H7 AGREE branch (see the two values below) and
  that this is ours to mutate for new cases without touching anything copied from
  upstream. Its sibling ProfiletoolHdrRefWhiteConflict holds the disagree branch.

  It satisfies every membership condition of 8.7.1.1 / 8.7.1.5:

    RGB data colour space                    (8.7.1.5 first sentence)
    ColorSpace class ('spac')                (8.7.1.5 second sentence)
    ProfileVersion 4.40, below 5.0.0.0       (icHdrIsVersion4 — a ruling, not a
                                              condition of the amendment; 4.7
                                              withdrew the old 4.5.0.0 floor)
    PCSXYZ                                   (the 8.7.1.2 chain ends in XYZ)
    cicpTag, TransferCharacteristics = 16    (8.7.1.1, PQ is one of 8/16/18)

  Deliberately a HAPPY PATH, not a torture test. The upstream fixtures cover the
  deformities (HdrInvalidTransfer, HdrMissingBToA0, HagcInvalidXOrder).

  Two values are set so they AGREE, which is the point of a happy path:
    - HAGC HDRReferenceWhite = 203.0 and metadata CRWL = 203.0. H7 asks whether
      those two carriers of the same quantity disagree; here they must not.
      (HagcColorSpace.icc uses 300.0 with no CRWL, so it cannot answer H7 either.)
    - ColourPrimaries = 9 (BT.2020). Under 8.7.1.1 the cicpTag is the ONLY carrier
      of the primaries — a ColorSpace profile has no matrix column tag — so the
      former redColorantTag/greenColorantTag/blueColorantTag trio is gone from this
      fixture. It was never required by the HDR clause; it was required of the
      matrix-based display profile that used to be the parent class.

  REGISTRY CAVEAT (inherited): the ICC dictType Metadata Registry that defines the
  CRWL/CLL/MDCV entry names and value syntax is unpublished, so those keys are
  reconstructions — see the ASSUMED markers in IccProfLib/IccHdrProfile.cpp. If the
  registry contradicts them, this fixture changes with the parser. The DERH/DRWL/DCV
  entries this fixture used to carry are gone with clause 8.10.5, which the
  23-09-2026 revision deleted: physical display characterization is out of scope for
  an HDR ColorSpace Profile.

  Generated through the iccxml WASM path (xmlToIcc), not by hand.
-->
<IccProfile>
  <Header>
    <PreferredCMMType>iccd</PreferredCMMType>
    <ProfileVersion>4.40</ProfileVersion>
    <ProfileDeviceClass>spac</ProfileDeviceClass>
    <DataColourSpace>RGB </DataColourSpace>
    <PCS>XYZ </PCS>
    <CreationDateTime>2026-09-10T00:00:00</CreationDateTime>
    <ProfileFlags EmbeddedInFile="true" UseWithEmbeddedDataOnly="true"/>
    <DeviceAttributes ReflectiveOrTransparency="reflective" GlossyOrMatte="glossy" MediaPolarity="positive" MediaColour="colour"/>
    <RenderingIntent>Relative Colorimetric</RenderingIntent>
    <PCSIlluminant>
      <XYZNumber X="0.964202880859" Y="1.000000000000" Z="0.824905395508"/>
    </PCSIlluminant>
    <ProfileCreator>iccd</ProfileCreator>
  </Header>
  <Tags>
    <!-- No TRC tags and no matrix column tags: clause 8.7 defines neither for a
         ColorSpace profile, so the cicpTag is the sole carrier of both the
         transfer function and the primaries (8.7.1.1). -->

    <mediaWhitePointTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.964202880859" Y="1.000000000000" Z="0.824905395508"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </mediaWhitePointTag>

    <cicpTag> <cicpType>
      <cicpFields ColorPrimaries="9" TransferCharacteristics="16" MatrixCoefficients="0" VideoFullRangeFlag="1"/>
    </cicpType> </cicpTag>

    <!-- Clause 8.7 requires the AToB0Tag/BToA0Tag pair of EVERY ColorSpace
         profile, and 8.7.1.5 constrains what the AToB0Tag must contain in an HDR
         ColorSpace Profile: an HDR->SDR rendering at target headroom 1.0, for a
         consumer that implements no HDR processing at all. The pair is the defect
         HdrMissingBToA0.icc isolates — critically now, since 8.7 owns it. Identity
         B-curve LUTs, exactly as HdrBakedLut.icc uses: what this fixture proves
         is that the pair is present and complete, not what it contains. -->
    <AToB0Tag> <lutAtoBType>
      <Channels InputChannels="3" OutputChannels="3"/>
      <BCurves>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
      </BCurves>
    </lutAtoBType> </AToB0Tag>

    <BToA0Tag> <lutBtoAType>
      <Channels InputChannels="3" OutputChannels="3"/>
      <BCurves>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
      </BCurves>
    </lutBtoAType> </BToA0Tag>

    <!-- A deliberately SIMPLE gain curve compared with HagcColorSpace's: one
         alternate, the fixed mixing type 2, PCHIP-derived slopes, and no custom
         chromaticities. The complex layout is already covered upstream; this one
         is here to be readable and to be mutated. HDRReferenceWhite is the
         203.0 default stated explicitly so it can be seen to agree with CRWL. -->
    <headroomAdaptiveGainCurveTag> <headroomAdaptiveGainCurveType>
      <HagcMetadata ApplicationVersion="1" MinApplicationVersion="1"
                    HDRReferenceWhite="203.0000"
                    BaselineHeadroom="2.0000" HeadroomAdaptiveToneMap="true"
                    ChromaticitiesMode="1" CommonComponentMixing="false" CommonCurveParameters="false">
       <AlternateImage Headroom="0.0000" ComponentMixingType="2" PchipSlope="true">
        <ControlPoints>
         <ControlPoint X="0.2500" Y="-0.05000"/>
         <ControlPoint X="0.5000" Y="-0.12000"/>
         <ControlPoint X="0.7500" Y="-0.20000"/>
         <ControlPoint X="1.0000" Y="-0.30000"/>
        </ControlPoints>
       </AlternateImage>
      </HagcMetadata>
    </headroomAdaptiveGainCurveType> </headroomAdaptiveGainCurveTag>

    <!-- CRWL matches the HAGC tag's HDRReferenceWhite above, which is what puts
         H7 on its AGREE branch (8.7.1.4). -->
    <metaDataTag> <dictType>
      <DictEntry Name="CRWL" Value="203.0"/>
    </dictType> </metaDataTag>

    <profileDescriptionTag> <multiLocalizedUnicodeType>
      <LocalizedText LanguageCountry="enUS"><![CDATA[profiletool conforming HDR ColorSpace Profile (BT.2020 PQ, HAGC)]]></LocalizedText>
    </multiLocalizedUnicodeType> </profileDescriptionTag>

    <copyrightTag> <multiLocalizedUnicodeType>
      <LocalizedText LanguageCountry="enUS"><![CDATA[Copyright (C) 2026 William Li. Generated fixture, no measured data.]]></LocalizedText>
    </multiLocalizedUnicodeType> </copyrightTag>
  </Tags>
</IccProfile>
